hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2953","Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) set out for Syria. When he reached the place called ""Sargh,"" he met the commander o"
"2954","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned the plague and said: ""It is a remnant of punishment. It is the punishment that was sent upon a group from the Children of Israel. When it occurs in a land and you are present there, do not flee from it, and when it occurs in another land, do not go there."
"2955","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Visit the sick, accompany funeral processions, these will remind you of the Hereafter."
"2956","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever visits a sick person, he remains immersed in mercy as long as he sits there, and as long as he sits, he is submerged in it."
"2957","Verily, when a Muslim visits his brother in Islam he is supposed to remain in the fruit garden of Paradise until he returns. (Using translation from Muslim 2568c)"
"2958","Are you visiting Hasan [during his sickness] when you feel what you feel? He said to him. Yes; you are not the Lord of my heart, to direct it as you wili. ʿAli ؓ said: That does not prevent me from giving you advice, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no Muslim who visits a [sick] Muslim, but Allah will send to him seventy thousand angels who will send blessings upon him from whatever hour of the day it is until evening comes, and from whatever hour of the night it is until morning comes.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 955)"
"2959","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) went to visit a Bedouin who was ill. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""There is no cause for worry; if Allah wills, it will be a means of purification."" But the man replied: ""No, rather it is a fever that is raging upon an old man and will take him to his grave."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Then it will be as you say."
"2960","I will intercede for you on the Day of Resurrection because of this."" The boy began to look towards his father, so his father said to him: ""Consider what Abu al-Qasim (peace be upon him) is telling you (i.e., obey him)."" So the boy said: ""I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) then said: ""All praise is due to Allah, who has saved him from the fire of Hell."
"2961","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""When a Muslim visits his Muslim brother who is ill or goes to meet him, Allah Almighty says: You remain pure and your walking remains pure; you have made your place of residence in Paradise."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narrator named Abu Sinan is Shaybani, and his name is Sa'id bin Sinan, while the narrator named Abu Sinan Kufi is Dhirar bin Murrah."
"2962","I used to recite the same supplication to seek cure for the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) that Angel Jibreel (peace be upon him) used to recite over the Prophet (peace be upon him) when he was ill (it is this): ""Remove the affliction, O Lord of the people, grant cure, there is no cure except Your cure, grant such a cure that leaves no illness behind."" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was afflicted with the illness in which he passed away, I began to recite this supplication over him, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Remove your hand, for this has benefited me for a long time."
"2963","“Whenever the Prophet ﷺ fell ill, he would recite the Mu’awwidhat and blow, and when his pain grew worse, I would recite over him and wipe his hand over him, hoping for its blessing.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3529)"
"2964","Place your hand at the place where you feel pain in your body and say Bismillah (in the name of Allah) three times and seven times A'udhu billahi wa qudratihi min sharri ma ajidu wa uhadhiru (I seek refuge with Allah and with His Power from the evil that I find and that I fear). (Using translation from Muslim 2202)"
"2965","I had a pain which was about to destroy me. So the Prophet ﷺ said : Wipe it with your right hand seven times and say : “I seek refuge in the dominance of Allah, and His might from the evil of what I find.” Then I did it. Allah removed (the pain) that I had, and I kept on suggesting it to my family and to others. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3891)"
"2966","""None of you should wish for death because of some harm that befalls him, rather he should say: 'Allahumma ahini ma kanatil-hayatu khairanli wa tawaffani idha kanatil-wafatu khairanli (O Allah, keep me alive so alive so long as life is good for me, and cause me to die when death is good for me.)""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1820)"
"2967","Place your hand at the place where you feel pain in your body and say Bismillah (in the name of Allah) three times and seven times A'udhu billahi wa qudratihi min sharri ma ajidu wa uhadhiru (I seek refuge with Allah and with His Power from the evil that I find and that I fear). (Using translation from Muslim 2202)"
"2968","I perform ruqyah for you, for every illness that troubles you, and for protection from the envy of the envier, and from every (evil) eye and poison. May Allah grant you healing."
"2969","narrates: Sayyidah Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) made a supplication: O Allah! Grant me blessings regarding my husband, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), my father Sayyiduna Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him), and my brother Mu’awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) (i.e., grant them long life). So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You have asked Allah regarding a matter whose time is fixed, whose signs will be reached, and whose sustenance has already been distributed. None of these things can be given before their appointed time. If you had asked Allah to save you from the punishment of Hell or the punishment of the grave, that would have been better (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words), that would have been superior."
"2970","I narrated this tradition to Mansur, so he narrated a similar narration from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"2971","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited ruqyah for a sick person, said: “Remove the hardship and suffering. Lord of mankind, and grant healing, for You are the Healer and there is no healing except Your healing; (grant) healing which does not leave any sickness behind.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 565)"
"2972","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited ruqyah for a sick person, said: “Remove the hardship and suffering. Lord of mankind, and grant healing, for You are the Healer and there is no healing except Your healing; (grant) healing which does not leave any sickness behind.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 565)"
"2973","“Bismillah, turbatu ardina, biriqati ba’dina, liyushfa saqimuna. Bi’dhni Rabbina (In the Name of Allah, the dust of our land mixed with the saliva of one of us, to cure our sick one by the permission of our Lord).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3521)"
"2974","narrates: Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would visit someone to inquire about his health, he (peace be upon him) would make this supplication: ""O Allah! Grant Your servant healing, so that he may blind the eye of the enemy for Your sake, or so that he may walk towards prayer for Your sake."
"2975","I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to grant you healing."" If the person's final moment was delayed, he would be granted well-being from that illness."
"2976","I remember that he (peace be upon him) recited this: ""So remove the pain, O Lord of the people."" And to the best of my knowledge, he (peace be upon him) also recited this: ""You are the only one who grants cure, only You can grant cure."
"2977","The firewood ran out, so I went out in search of wood. You grabbed the pot and poured it over your wrist. I took you to the service of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! This is Muhammad bin Hatib, and he is the first child whose name has been kept after your blessed name. Sayyidah Umm Jameel (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his blessed saliva in your mouth, passed his blessed hand over your head, and prayed for you, and said: ""Remove the pain, O Lord of the people! Grant healing, You are the only healer. There is no healing except Your healing, grant such a healing that leaves no illness behind."" Sayyidah Umm Jameel (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I had not yet risen with you from the service of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when your hand was healed."
"2978","I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to grant you healing."" If the person's appointed time was not near, he would recover from that illness."
"2979","narrates this statement of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Whoever Allah grants sixty years of age, then regarding age, He leaves no excuse remaining for him."
"2980","“The ages of (the people in) my nation will be between sixty and seventy, and few of them will exceed that.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4236)"
"2981","The people said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best among you are those whose lives are long and whose deeds are good."
"2982","The one who was more diligent participated in battle and attained martyrdom. The other man lived for another year, during which he also fasted in Ramadan, and then he passed away. Once, Sayyiduna Talhah bin Ubaidullah (may Allah be pleased with him) saw in a dream that a person came out from Paradise and permitted entry to the one who had died later among the two. Then that person came out from Paradise again and permitted entry to the one who had been martyred. Then he returned to Sayyiduna Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: ""You go back, your time has not yet come."" The next day, Sayyiduna Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) discussed this matter with people. News of this reached the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). The people informed him and expressed their amazement. They said: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! That person was more diligent among the two and he was also martyred in the way of Allah, but this (other one) entered Paradise before him."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Did he not live for another year after him?"" The people replied: ""Yes."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Did he not witness the month of Ramadan and fast in it, and did he not offer so many prayers in the mosque throughout the year?"" The people replied: ""Yes."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That is why the difference between them is greater than the distance between the sky and the earth."" The narrator named Abu Salamah passed away in 94 Hijri, while Sayyiduna Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred in the Battle of Jamal in the year 36 Hijri."
"2983","That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever develops some gray hair in the cause of Allah, it shall be a light for him in the Day of Judgement. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1635)"
"2984","""O Ka'b bin Murrah! Relate (something) to is from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and be cautious. He said: 'I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ""Whoever develops some gray hair in Islam, it shall be a light from him on the Day of Judgement."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1634)"
"2985","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Do not pluck out white hairs, for they will be light on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever grows old in Islam (i.e., his hair turns white), good deeds will be written for him in exchange for them, his sins will be forgiven in exchange for them, and his ranks will be elevated in exchange for them."
"2986","There would be none amongst the created beings living on the earth (who would survive this century). (Using translation from Muslim 2539)"
"2987","I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying this one month before his death: You asked me about the Last Hour whereas its knowledge is with Allah. I, however, take an oath and say that none upon the earth, the created beings (from amongst my Companions), would survive at the end of one hundred years. (Using translation from Muslim 2538a)"
"2988","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You people ask me about the Hour (Day of Judgment). By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, there will not remain any living person on the face of the earth one hundred years from today."
"2989","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the ‘Isha prayer during the last days of his life. When he finished the prayer with salam, he stood up and said: Do you know about this night of yours? Exactly one hundred years from today, none of those who are present on the face of the earth now will remain."
"2990","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever among you is alive today, after one hundred years none of them will remain alive."
"2991","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""You people ask me about the Hour (Day of Judgment). By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, there will not remain any living person on the face of the earth alive after one hundred years from today."
"2992","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Frequently remember the destroyer of pleasures,’ meaning death.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4258)"
"2993","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: \""Remember frequently the destroyer of pleasures. Whoever remembers it in times of hardship, it becomes ease for him, and whoever remembers it in times of ease, it brings constriction upon him.\"""""
"2994","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Remember frequently the destroyer of pleasures (i.e., death).\"""""
"2995","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would often say: ""Remember frequently the thing which ends all pleasures."
"2996","The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: O Abdullah! What is this? I replied: We are repairing our shelter. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: The Day of Judgment will come even faster than this."
"2997","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon me when we were repairing our cottage that was broken. He asked: What is this? We replied: This cottage of ours has broken and we are repairing it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I see that the command is quicker than that. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5236)"
"2998","""This is the son of Adam, and this is his life-span."" And he placed his hand at the (height of the) nape of his neck, then he extended it (higher) and said:"" From there is what is hoped for, from there is what is hoped for."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2334)"
"2999","I would have prayed for it."" Then he mentioned his companions who had departed (from this world), saying, ""These people have gone and did not receive any worldly benefit from their reward, and after them, we remained and acquired the world. None of us knows what to do with it except to spend it on earth (i.e., on construction), and a Muslim is rewarded for everything he spends except for what he spends on earth (i.e., on construction)."
"3000","""None of you should wish for death. Either he is a doer of good, so perhaps he may do more good, or he is an evildoer but perhaps he will give up his evil ways."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1818)"
"3001","“None of you should wish for death because of some harm that befalls him. If he must wish for death, let him say: ‘O Allah, keep me alive so long as living is good for me and cause me to die when death is good for me.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4265)"
"3002","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite Surah Yasin over your dying ones."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Recite it over your dead,"" means: Recite Surah Yasin over the person whose final moments have approached, because recitation is not done over the dead. Similarly, the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Instruct your dead to say La ilaha illallah"" (i.e., instruct those near death to say it)."
"3003","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Recite to those of you who are dying ""There is no god but Allah."" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3117)"
"3004","Exhort to recite"" There is no god but Allah"" to those of you who are dying. (Using translation from Muslim 916a)"
"3005","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ: When you attend dying man, you should say good words, for the angels say Amin to what you say. When Abu Salamah died, I said: What should I say, Messenger of Allah? He said: O Allah forgive him, and give us something good in exchange. She said: So Allah gave me Muhammad ﷺ in exchange for him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3115)"
"3006","I became concerned that this might cause difficulty for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so someone said to another: ""By Allah! Now we will not inform the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about anyone until he has passed away. When he passes away, then we will inform the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so that he does not have to face hardship in this regard and does not have to stay for a long time."" The narrator says: We did exactly that. After that, we started informing the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) after the person had passed away. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would come to that person, supplicate for mercy for him, and supplicate for his forgiveness. Sometimes, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would return immediately, and sometimes he would stay until the deceased was buried. The narrator says: We continued to do this for a while, then we thought, ""By Allah! Now we will not call the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), rather we will carry our dead to the funeral, so that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) can perform the funeral prayer near his house. This will be easier and more convenient for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."" So we started doing this, and it has continued like this until today."
"3007","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Either he has found relief or relief has been found from him. We asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! How has he found relief or how has relief been found from him? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When a believer passes away, he finds relief from the hardships, worries, and troubles of the world. And when a disbeliever passes away, people, cities, trees, and animals find relief from him."
"3008","He who loves to meet Allah, Allah also loves to meet him, and he who dislikes to meet Allah, Allah also abhors to meet him. (Using translation from Muslim 2683a)"
"3009","The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6508)"
"3010","He who loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him, and he who dislikes to meet Allah, Allah abhors to meet him. I ('A'isha) said: Allah's Apostle, so far as the feeling of aversion against death is concerned, we all have this feeling. Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: It is not that (which you construe), but (this) that when a believer (at the time of death) is given the glad tidings of the mercy of Allah, His Pleasure, and of Paradise, he loves to meet Allah, and Allah also loves to meet him, and when an unbeliever is given the news of the torment at the Hand of Allah, and Hardship to be imposed by Him, he dislikes to meet Allah and Allah also abhors to meet him. (Using translation from Muslim 2684a)"
"3011","The death of a believer occurs with sweat on the forehead."
"3012","A funeral procession passed by Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said, ""Relieved or relieving?"" The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! What is relieved and relieving?"" He said, ""A believer is relieved (by death) from the troubles and hardships of the world and leaves for the Mercy of Allah, while (the death of) a wicked person relieves the people, the land, the trees, (and) the animals from him."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6512)"
"3013","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): When the final moment of a believer approaches, the angels of mercy come to him. When his soul is taken, it is placed in a white garment. The angels then take it towards the gate of the sky. The (angels of the first heaven) say: We have never smelled a fragrance purer than this. Then it is said: Leave him, he has attained comfort, for previously he was in the grief (of th"
"3014","The angels say this at every sky they pass, until they bring it to the souls of the believers. Then those souls rejoice at meeting it just as the family of an absent person rejoices at his return. They say: 'What is the condition of so-and-so?' Then others say: 'Leave him, let him rest, for he was in the distress of the world.' Then the (deceased) says: 'What about so-and-so?' They say: 'He has passed away, has he not come to you?' They say: 'He must have been taken to his abode in Hawiyah.' (The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, says:) As for the disbeliever, the angels of punishment come to him with a coarse, rough cloth and say: 'Come out towards the wrath of Allah.' So the soul comes out as if it is the foulest stench of a decaying corpse, and they bring it to the gate of the earth."",""When a believer passes away"",""angels of mercy come to him with white silk covers and say: 'Come out to the mercy of Allah.' So"","" his soul comes out like the sweetest fragrance of musk till they reach the nearest heaven. They ask permission to enter and Allah grants them permission. In every heaven"","" they ask for his permission and it is granted until they reach the seventh heaven. Then Allah says: [Record the book of My slave in 'Illiyyin and take him back to the earth"","" for I created them from it"","" and I shall return them into it and from it I shall extract them a second time] [23.12-14]. At that point"","" his soul is returned to his body and two angels come and make him sit up."""""",""Regarding disbelievers"",""angels of punishment come to them with sackcloth and say: """"Come out to the wrath of Allah."""" Then"","" his soul disperses like the most foul stench imaginable"","" and they take it up to the lowest heaven. They ask permission to enter and Allah does not give them permission."""
"3015","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""No person should wish for death, nor should he pray for it before it comes, because when he passes away, his deeds will be cut off, and the life of a believer only increases him in goodness."
"3016","When a man dies, his acts come to an end, but three, recurring charity, or knowledge (by which people) benefit, or a pious son, who prays for him (for the deceased). (Using translation from Muslim 1631)"
"3017","I do not know. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) migrated to Madinah Munawwarah, Sayyiduna Tufail bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) also migrated and came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). With him was a man from his tribe. That man suffered from severe fever and began to weep and wail. He took a knife and cut his vein with it, and his blood began to flow until he died. He was buried. Then, at night, a person came to Sayyiduna Tufail bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) in a dream, who was in a very excellent appearance and had covered his hand. Tufail asked him: Are you so-and-so? He replied: Yes. Sayyiduna Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: How are you? He said: My Lord has treated me excellently and has forgiven me because of my migration to His Prophet. Sayyiduna Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: What happened to your hand? He replied: My Lord said to me: We will never fix what you yourself have ruined. The narrator says: Sayyiduna Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) related this dream to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised both his hands (and supplicated): “O Allah! Forgive both his hands as well. O Allah! Forgive both his hands as well. O Allah! Forgive his both hands as well.”"",""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Medina"",""Al-Tufayl ibn 'Amr came to him as an emigrant"","" accompanied by a man from his tribe. This man contracted a severe fever"","" which caused him great distress"","" so he became anxious and took a knife and slit his veins"","" causing himself to bleed excessively until he died. He was buried"","" and it was mentioned in what the sleeping person sees at night that Al-Tufayl ibn 'Amr would come to him in a good state"","" with his hands tied. So the sleeping person said to him"","" """"Is so-and-so (mentioning the man who died) okay?"""" He replied"","" """"Yes."""" He asked him"","" """"What did you do?"""" He replied"","" """"My Lord did good to me and forgave me through my migration to His Prophet ﷺ."""" The sleeping person asked him"","" """"What did you do with your hands?"""" He replied"","" """"My Lord said to me"","" 'We will not rectify from you what you have corrupted of yourself.'"""" Al-Tufayl then narrated this dream to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands and supplicated"","" saying"","" """"O Allah"","" be merciful to him and his hands. O Allah"","" be merciful to him and his hands. O Allah"","" be merciful to him and his hands."""""""
"3018","When your companion dies, leave him and do not revile him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4899)"
"3019","When your companion dies, leave him and do not revile him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4899)"
"3020","The Prophet ﷺ said: Make a mention of the virtues of your dead, and refrain from (mentioning) their evils. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4900)"
"3021","I seek forgiveness from Allah."" People asked Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), ""What is the reason that first you cursed him and then you said, 'I seek forgiveness from Allah'?"" So Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) explained that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not speak ill of the dead, for they have gone on to what they sent forth."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) passed away in 57 Hijri, and Mujahid was born in the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) in 21 Hijri, so this will guide you to the fact that whoever claims that Mujahid did not hear hadith from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), he is mistaken in his opinion."
"3022","""Do not vilify the dead (and) by that harm the living."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1982)"
"3023","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It has become obligatory."" Then people passed by with another funeral, and the people praised it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It has become obligatory."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! What has become obligatory?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These people passed by with him and mentioned his evil, so Hell became obligatory for him. These people passed by with him and mentioned his praise, so Paradise became obligatory for him. You are Allah's witnesses on earth."
"3024","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It has become obligatory. You are Allah's witnesses on earth."
"3025","“A funeral (procession) passed by the Prophet ﷺ and they praised (the deceased) and spoke well of him. He said: ‘(Paradise is) guaranteed for him.’ Then another funeral passed by and they spoke badly of him, and he (the Prophet ﷺ) said: ‘(Hell is) guaranteed for him.’ It was said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, you said that (Paradise was) guaranteed for this one and that (Hell was) guaranteed for the other one.’ He said: ‘It is the testimony of the people, and the believers are the witnesses of Allah on earth.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1491)"
"3026","I have accepted your knowledge about this person, and I have forgiven those things of his which you do not know."
"3027","The people spoke ill of him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It has become obligatory."" Then people passed by with another funeral and spoke well of him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It has become obligatory."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about this, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are Allah's witnesses on earth."
"3028","I came to Madinah and found that sickness was occurring in it and death was widespread. I sat with 'Umar bin al-Khattab and a funeral passed by him. People spoke well of the deceased and ‘Umar said: It is guaranteed. Then another funeral passed by and people spoke well of the deceased and ‘Umar said: It is guaranteed. Then a third funeral passed by and people spoke badly of the deceased and ‘Umar said: It is guaranteed. Abul-Aswad said: What is guaranteed, O Ameer al-Mu'mineen? He said: I am saying what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿAny Muslim in whose favour four people testify, Allah will admit him to Paradise.ʿ We said: And three? He said: ʿAnd three.ʿ We said: And two? He said: ʿAnd two ʿ Then we did not ask him about one. (Using translation from Aḥmad 139)"
"3029","It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas and ‘Aishah that Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet ﷺ when he died. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1457)"
"3030","narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) entered the mosque at a time when Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was talking with the people. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) went inside the house where the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had passed away. This was the house of the noble wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) removed the sheet made of ""Habrah"" with which the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had been covered. He looked at the blessed face of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), then leaned over him and kissed him, and said: ""May my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! By Allah, Allah will not combine two deaths upon you. You have tasted the death after which you will never die."
"3031","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you place stones (in the grave) for the deceased, place them in an odd numb"
"3032","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us while we were washing his daughter. He said: Wash her with water and lote tree leaves"
"3033","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us when we were washing his daughter Umm Kulthum. He said: ‘Wash her three or five times, or more than that if you think you need to, with water and lote leaves, and put camphor or a little camphor in (the water) for the last washing. When you have finished, call for me.’ When we finished, we called him, and he gave his waist-wrapper to us and said: ‘Shroud her with it.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1458)"
"3034","Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day in the course of his sermon made mention of a person among his Companions who had died and had been wrapped in a shroud not long (enough to cover his whole body) and was buried during the night. The Apostle of Allah ﷺ reprimanded (the audience) that a person was buried during the night (in a state that) funeral prayer could not be offered (over him by the Messenger of Allah). (And this is permissible only) when it becomes a dire necessity for a man. The Apostle of Allah ﷺ also said: When any one of you shrouds his brother, he should shroud him well. (Using translation from Muslim 943)"
"3035","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was shrouded in two ""Sahouli"" garments."
"3036","The one whose tears always remain held back, soon they will burst forth."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O my daughter! Do not say this, rather recite this (which is a verse from the Qur'an): ""The stupor of death has come in truth; this is what you were trying to avoid."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) inquired: In how many garments was the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) shrouded? I replied: In three garments. So he said: Shroud me in these two of my garments and buy a new cloth along with them, because a living person is more in need of new clothes than a deceased one. These are working clothes (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) or clothes for respite."
"3037","""The Prophet was shrouded in three white Suhuli garments."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1898)"
"3038","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'When the Janazah (prepared body) is placed (on the bier) and the men lift it onto their shoulders, if it was a righteous person it says: Take me quickly, take me quickly. And if it was not a righteous person it says: Woe to me! Where are you taking me! And everything hears its voice except man, and if man heard it he would faint.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1909)"
"3039","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'When the Janazah (prepared body) is placed (on the bier) and the men lift it onto their shoulders, if it was a righteous person it says: Take me quickly, take me quickly. And if it was not a righteous person it says: Woe to me! Where are you taking me! And everything hears its voice except man, and if man heard it he would faint.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1909)"
"3040","""The Messenger of Allah commanded us to do seven things: He commanded us to attend funerals, visit the sick, to reply (say: Yarhamuk Allah [may Allah have mercy on you]) to one who sneezes, to accept invitations, to support the oppressed, to fulfill oaths (when adjured by another) and to return greetings of Salaam."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3778)"
"3041","I am the messenger of Allah’s Messenger (peace be upon him) who has come to you. Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: We said: Welcome to Allah’s Messenger (peace be upon him) and to the messenger of Allah’s Messenger (peace be upon him). Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You women should pledge that you will not associate anything with Allah, nor commit adultery, nor steal. He recited this verse. Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: We replied: Yes. Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: He extended his hand from the outer part of the house and we extended our hands from the inner part of the house. Then he said: O Allah! Bear witness. Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) commanded us regarding Eid that we should bring out even the adult and free women on this occasion, but Jumu’ah is not obligatory upon us women, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade us from accompanying funeral processions. The narrator named Ismail says: I asked my grandmother (Lady Umm Atiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her) about the statement of Allah the Exalted: “And that they will not disobey you in what is right.” She said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade us from wailing."
"3042","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: Walk quickly with a funeral, for if the dead person was good it is a good condition to which you are sending him on, but it he was otherwise it is an evil of which you are riding yourselves. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3181)"
"3043","The narrator says: So the people came and started walking quickly, and Ziyad also started walking quickly."
"3044","I remember this about myself that I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I used to walk with the funerals in such a way as if running."
"3045","That his father saw the Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr and 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, walking in front of the Janazah. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1944)"
"3046","I saw the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr and Umar walking before the funeral. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3179)"
"3047","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) walking in front of the funeral procession. Sufyan, the narrator, was asked: In the narration, are these the words, ""and I also saw Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)""? He replied: I do not remember these words. He was asked: Some people say that this narration is transmitted from Salim, so he said: Zuhri narrated this to us several times, and I testify before you to this. He was asked: Ibn Jurayj narrates this hadith in the same way as you do, but he also mentions Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) in it. Sufyan said: I did not hear him mention Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3048","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) also used to walk in front of the funeral procession. Zuhri narrates: This is also the Sunnah."
"3049","""The Messenger of Allah said: The riders should move behind the Janazah and the pedestrian may walk wherever he wishes, and the (funeral) prayer should be offered for a child.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1942)"
"3050","We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a funeral passed hi and he stood up for it. When we went to carry it, we found that it was a funeral of a Jew. We, therefore said: Messenger of Allah, this is the funeral of a Jew. He said: Death is fearful event, so when you see a funeral, stand up. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3174)"
"3051","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: When you see a funeral, stand up for it till it leaves you behind or it is placed (on the ground). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3172)"
"3052","""When you see a funeral, stand up until it has passed you, or (the body) is placed (in the grave)."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1916)"
"3053","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes, stand for it, because you are not standing for the deceased, but rather you are standing out of respect for the one who seizes the soul."
"3054","narrates: Previously (it was the practice of the Prophet ) that when he saw a funeral, he would stand up; (later, the Prophet adopted this practice) that he would remain seated."
"3055","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to stand upon seeing a funeral, until it was placed (on the ground), then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would sit down."
"3056","I saw a funeral among Banu Salimah so I stood up. Nafi’ bin Jubair said to me: Sit down, and I will tell you something decisive about this: Masʿood bin al-Hakam az-Zuraqi told me that he heard ‘Ali bin Abi Talib ؓ in Rahbatal-Koofah saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us to stand up for funerals; then later on he remained seated and told us to remain seated. (Using translation from Aḥmad 623)"
"3057","The Prophet (peace be upon him) did not perform the funeral prayer for the person whose description we have mentioned. His purpose in this was to teach his Ummah proper etiquette in this regard, so that they would avoid committing such acts. This does not mean that it is not permissible at all to perform the funeral prayer for a person who possesses the characteristic for which the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not perform the funeral prayer."
"3058","The Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired: ""Does he have any debt?"" The people replied: ""Yes, two dinars."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: ""Did he leave anything for its repayment?"" The people replied: ""No."" So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""You perform the funeral prayer of your companion."" Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! The repayment of both is upon me."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed his funeral prayer."
"3059","The Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired: “Does he have any debt?” The people replied: “He owes two dinars.” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “You perform the funeral prayer of your companion.” Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! The payment of these two (dinars) is upon me.” So the Prophet (peace be upon him) stepped forward and led the funeral prayer for him."
"3060","“I heard 'Abdullah bin Abu Qatadah narrate from his father that a corpse was brought to the Prophet ﷺ for him to offer the funeral prayer, and he said: 'Pray for your companion, for he owes a debt.' Abu Qatadah said: 'I will stand surely for him?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'In full?' He said: 'In full.” And the debt he owed was eighteen or nineteen Dirham.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2407)"
"3061","The soul of the believer remains suspended until his debt is paid off."
"3062","I am closer to the believers than their own selves. Whoever leaves behind wealth, it will go to his family, and whoever leaves behind debt or dependents, their payment is my responsibility or they are entrusted to me, because I am closer to the believers."
"3063","if a believer died at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he had debts, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would ask: “Did he leave anything with which to off his debt?” If they said yes, then he would offer the funeral prayer for him, but if they said no, then he would say: “Pray for your companion.” When Allah granted his Prophet ﷺ the conquests, he said: “I am nearer to the believers than their own selves. Whoever dies owing a debt, I will pay it off for him, and whoever leaves behind wealth, it will be for his heirs.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2415)"
"3064","I take responsibility for its payment."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed his funeral prayer. When Allah Almighty granted His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) conquests, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am closer to every believer than his own self. So whoever leaves behind a debt, its payment is my responsibility, and whoever leaves behind wealth, it will go to his heirs."
"3065","I swear by Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over Suhail b. al-Baida' in the mosque. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3189)"
"3066","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the funeral prayer of Sayyiduna Sahl bin Bayda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) in the mosque."
